# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Served before static files, and a fragment never
# reaches the server at all — the browser re-applies it to the target, so
# /claims#transportation lands on /search#transportation. (Verified in Chromium
# against a local 301 on 2026-09-03: the server logged the path without the
# fragment, the browser finished on the target with the fragment intact.)
#
# `redirects.yaml` is the source of truth for where published addresses go
# under D-0029, and this file is to be generated from it. The rule below is the
# one address already live, kept as it stands because its D-0029 target
# (/questions) does not exist yet.
/claims /search 301
